        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T09:18:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should we `Some(1) \u003d\u003e Ok(true)` and still `warn!` (not `debug!`) on other values (`Some(n)`)? Or is it valid to define bool-like DT values as true for any non-zero value?\n\nIf so, I think we should log the unexpected value:\n```\nwarn!(\"Unexpected value for debug policy property /avf/guest/common/ramdump: {n}\")\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 149,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "7ac3b225fa2cf67bb2b2895ab578926a7cab617d",
