    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f1141a0_3433506e",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/debug_policy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 153,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T09:18:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Move these 2 `debug` statements to the caller so that we handle all paths that could return `true` or `false`, limit the number of functions that are logging, and possibly detect redundant logging calls.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 153,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 153,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "7ac3b225fa2cf67bb2b2895ab578926a7cab617d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef8342f8_a122b745",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/debug_policy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 153,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T16:36:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree to limit log number for `error` or `warn`, but disagree for `debug`. Isn\u0027t `debug` for intended verbose log because of development purpose?",
      "parentUuid": "3f1141a0_3433506e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 153,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 153,
        "endChar": 85
      },
      "revId": "7ac3b225fa2cf67bb2b2895ab578926a7cab617d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31128e04_41b1690a",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/debug_policy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T09:18:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "(comment originally written for the `warn` of PS2 but still applicable, IMO)\n\nSo `handle_debug_policy` is always called because it patches the DT (`handle_ramdump`) even if we don\u0027t have a DP (`debug_policy\u003d\u003dNone`) but it isn\u0027t an error for a vendor to distribute pvmfw without DP so shouldn\u0027t this be a `debug!` instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7ac3b225fa2cf67bb2b2895ab578926a7cab617d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "775fa5ac_66c1f408",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/debug_policy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 173,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T16:36:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re correct, because dpm partition can be erased and device can boot without dpm.bin. Pixel team thinks \u0027no dpm\u0027 isn\u0027t a normal situation and shouldn\u0027t be considered as normal case, but I think that vendors may want to ship device without AVF debug policy.\n\nFeel free to reopen if it seems wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "31128e04_41b1690a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 173,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 173,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "7ac3b225fa2cf67bb2b2895ab578926a7cab617d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d857afd4_024f257c",
        "filename": "pvmfw/src/debug_policy.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 174,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882526
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-20T09:18:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI, if you wrote this `if`-`else` because a `match` on the `Option` felt overkill (it is!), Rust\u0027s solution is the `if let` statement:\n```\nif let Some(dp) \u003d debug_policy {\n    apply_debug_policy(fdt, dp)?;\n} else {\n    // ...\n}\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 174,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "7ac3b225fa2cf67bb2b2895ab578926a7cab617d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
